module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_green_case_set_that_counts_row_identities_and_never_the_branches_those_rows_take

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// AN INSTRUMENT WHOSE CASE ROWS ARE COUNTED BY IDENTITY REPORTS GREEN OVER A SUBJECT WHOSE BRANCHES WERE
// NEVER ENTERED. The cases ran, each one held, and the receipt said something true about the ROSTER and
// nothing about the code. Filed 2026-10-31 by proud-bear-756 at the manager's direction (calm-crab-645,
// msg_b18efa42), naming as its first instance the receipt this author produced personally: 53 of 53 held at
// 50043a419018734c846f483c06fb97cc68335fa0, and that head carried the two defects filed as
// 'a_request_rewrite_that_reencodes_the_body_it_edits_reorders_the_keys_downstream_reads' and
// 'a_counter_acquired_under_one_predicate_and_released_under_another_goes_negative'.

data a_green_case_set_that_counts_row_identities_and_never_the_branches_those_rows_take: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_green_case_set_that_counts_row_identities_and_never_the_branches_those_rows_take" as NonEmptyStr,

  // FOUND SILENTLY WRONG: the green verdict was not even a wrong VERDICT, it was a true verdict about the
  // wrong object, which is why no one contradicted it. The ceiling is MechanicallyPreventable because the
  // refusing construction has already been run once by hand (the control receipt below), not because a
  // mechanism is on the required path.
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the capability of an instrument to record, per case row, which clause of its subject that row enters, and to refuse a roster that leaves a declared clause of the subject unentered -- for the router proxy falsifier, the axes its own dev-world map already names (cache locality, per-upstream cap including the zero sentinel, in-service, pinned, overflow) -- so that a green run is a statement about the subject and not a restatement of which cases the author thought of"
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**INVALID STATE.** Every declared case identity holds, the identity count matches the declared row count,
    the process exits zero -- and the behaviour that is broken was never exercised. The count is over
    IDENTITIES, and identities are authored by the same hand that wrote the subject, so a green count is a
    statement about the author's attention, re-derived and re-reported. Nothing in the instrument records what
    each case ENTERED, so the only coverage fact available is the roster itself.",

    "**THE INSTANCE, MEASURED.** The 2026-10-30 srv1 receipt at 50043a419018734c846f483c06fb97cc68335fa0: 53
    falsifier identities == 53 declared rows (set-compared, not counted), 53 held, 0 not held, exit zero, run
    as an on-host job. The head was broken twice: an alias rewrite that re-encoded the whole forwarded body,
    and a bound engine-local arm that released a turn it had never reserved. NEITHER BRANCH WAS REACHED. Both
    byte-fidelity cases sent a DIRECT model id, so the rewrite predicate was false and the branch did not run;
    no fixture row was simultaneously engine_local and cap 0, so the arm that skipped the reservation did not
    run either. The receipt was accurate and, for the decision it was used in, worthless.",

    "**WHY IT LOOKED SAFE -- AND WHY THE INSTRUMENT IS NOT THE CULPRIT.** That falsifier is a real instrument:
    it emits the proxy from the model, starts containers, drives requests, and reads back counters; it caught
    several genuine defects the same week. What is missing is not rigour but a COVERAGE OBJECT: the case set
    has no field saying which subject clause each case is responsible for, so coverage can only be argued in
    prose, and prose about a roster always reads back green.",

    "**THE CONTROL THAT MAKES A RECEIPT SAY SOMETHING ABOUT THE SUBJECT (as executed, calm-moth-166, srv1).**
    Take the fixed tree and restore ONE file -- router_dev_policy.dag at the pre-fix revision -- leaving the
    instrument untouched. Exactly the four newest cases fail and every other case holds. That run is the shape
    this row demands of a receipt: a body change to the subject MOVES the verdict, on a case set chosen to move.
    A run that cannot be moved by the defect it is offered as evidence for is a run over the roster.",

    "**NOT A DUPLICATE OF THE ADJACENT ROWS.** 'green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own' is
    about a population whose AUTHORITY is wrong; 'green_floor_executes_no_claim_whose_verdict_a_body_change_can_move'
    is about a required floor whose STATIC roster omits affected claims; 'a_rust_test_target_that_does_not_compile_reads_green'
    is about a check that never ran at all. None of them is this: here the cases ran, and held, and were green,
    and the branch that broke was never entered by any of them.",

    "**CEILING AND TRIGGER.** MechanicallyPreventable. The construction is a coverage obligation carried as
    data -- per case, the subject clause it enters; per instrument, a refusal over clauses no case enters --
    and the falsifier's own dev-world map already enumerates the router's axes, so the obligation is writable
    today. Blocker ClimbableButUnbuilt: nothing waits on an authority or a new capability; what is missing is a
    lane that builds the obligation and puts the run on the required path, since CI's v2-bootstrap executes no
    claim rows and a hand-run receipt -- however careful -- is exactly what this row indicts.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.router_proxy_falsifier", decl_name: "falsifier_cases"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.router_proxy_falsifier", decl_name: "row_cases"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.router_dev_scaffold", decl_name: "router_dev_policy_scaffold"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.std.subject_evidence", decl_name: "subject_evidence_establishes"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_request_rewrite_that_reencodes_the_body_it_edits_reorders_the_keys_downstream_reads", decl_name: "a_request_rewrite_that_reencodes_the_body_it_edits_reorders_the_keys_downstream_reads"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_counter_acquired_under_one_predicate_and_released_under_another_goes_negative", decl_name: "a_counter_acquired_under_one_predicate_and_released_under_another_goes_negative"),
  ],
}
